groundColor: '#fff3cd',\n        border: '1px solid #ffc107',\n        borderRadius: '4px',\n        margin: '1rem 0'\n      }}\n    >\n      <div style={{ \n        fontSize: '32px', \n        marginBottom: '1rem',\n        color: '#856404'\n      }}>\n        ⚠️\n      </div>\n      <p style={{ \n        color: '#856404', \n        fontSize: '14px',\n        marginBottom: '1rem',\n        textAlign: 'center',\n        maxWidth: '500px'\n      }}>\n        {message}\n      </p>\n      <div style={{ fontSize: '12px', color: '#856404', marginBottom: '1rem' }}>\n        <ul style={{ textAlign: 'left', paddingLeft: '1.5rem' }}>\n          <li>Check your network connection</li>\n          <li>Verify the API server is running</li>\n          <li>Contact support if the issue persists</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      {onRetry && (\n        <button \n          onClick={onRetry}\n          style={{\n            padding: '0.5rem 1rem',\n            backgroundColor: '#ffc107',\n            border: 'none',\n            borderRadius: '4px',\n            cursor: 'pointer',\n            fontSize: '14px',\n            color: '#856404',\n            fontWeight: 'bold'\n          }}\n        >\n          Retry\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\nEOF\n\n# Create Empty state component\ncat > src/components/states/EmptyState.tsx << 'EOF'\nimport React from 'react';\n\ninterface EmptyStateProps {\n  message?: string;\n  icon?: string;\n}\n\nexport const EmptyState: React.FC<EmptyStateProps> = ({ \n  message = 'No tasks found',\n  icon = '📋'\n}) => {\n  return (\n    <div \n      className=\"empty-state\"\n      style={{\n        display: 'flex',\n        flexDirection: 'column',\n        alignItems: 'center',\n        justifyContent: 'center',\n        padding: '3rem',\n        minHeight: '200px',\n        backgroundColor: '#f8f9fa',\n        border: '1px solid #dee2e6',\n        borderRadius: '4px'\n      }}\n    >\n      <div style={{ \n        fontSize: '48px', \n        marginBottom: '1rem',\n        opacity: 0.5\n      }}>\n        {icon}\n      </div>\n      <p style={{ \n        color: '#6c757d', \n        fontSize: '14px',\n        margin: 0\n      }}>\n        {message}\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\nEOF\n\n# Create index file for state components\ncat > src/components/states/index.ts << 'EOF'\nexport { LoadingState } from './LoadingState';\nexport { ErrorState } from './ErrorState';\nexport { EmptyState } from './EmptyState';\nEOF\n\n# Update Dashboard component to use new state components\ncat > src/components/Dashboard.tsx << 'EOF'\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\nimport { LoadingState, ErrorState, EmptyState } from './states';\nimport { TaskTable } from './TaskTable';\nimport { RunSummary } from './RunSummary';\n\ninterface Task {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  status: string;\n  [key: string]: any;\n}\n\ninterface DashboardData {\n  tasks: Task[];\n  summary: any;\n}\n\nexport const Dashboard: React.FC = () => {\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState<boolean>(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null);\n  const [data, setData] = useState<DashboardData | null>(null);\n\n  const fetchData = async () => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    setError(null);\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch('/api/dashboard');\n      if (!response.ok) {\n        throw new Error('Failed to fetch dashboard data');\n      }\n      const result = await response.json();\n      setData(result);\n    } catch (err) {\n      setError(err as Error);\n    } finally {\n      setLoading(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    fetchData();\n  }, []);\n\n  if (loading) {\n    return <LoadingState message=\"Loading dashboard...\" />;\n  }\n\n  if (error) {\n    return <ErrorState onRetry={fetchData} />;\n  }\n\n  if (!data) {\n    return <ErrorState message=\"No data available\" />;\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"dashboard\">\n      <h1>Dashboard</h1>\n      \n      {data.summary && <RunSummary summary={data.summary} />}\n      \n      <div className=\"tasks-section\">\n        <h2>Tasks</h2>\n        {data.tasks.length === 0 ? (\n          <EmptyState message=\"No tasks found\" icon=\"📋\" />\n        ) : (\n          <TaskTable tasks={data.tasks} />\n        )}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\nEOF\n\n# Create tests for state components\nmkdir -p src/components/states/__tests__\n\ncat > src/components/states/__tests__/LoadingState.test.tsx << 'EOF'\nimport React from 'react';\nimport { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { LoadingState } from '../LoadingState';\n\ndescribe('LoadingState', () => {\n  it('renders default loading message', () => {\n    render(<LoadingState />);\n    expect(screen.getByText('Loading dashboard...')).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it('renders custom loading message', () => {\n    render(<LoadingState message=\"Loading tasks...\" />);\n    expect(screen.getByText('Loading tasks...')).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it('has proper accessibility attributes', () => {\n    render(<LoadingState />);\n    const loadingDiv = screen.getByRole('status');\n    expect(loadingDiv).toHaveAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');\n  });\n\n  it('renders spinner element', () => {\n    const { container } = render(<LoadingState />);\n    const spinner = container.querySelector('.spinner');\n    expect(spinner).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\nEOF\n\ncat > src/components/states/__tests__/ErrorState.test.tsx << 'EOF'\nimport React from 'react';\nimport { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { ErrorState } from '../ErrorState';\n\ndescribe('ErrorState', () => {\n  it('renders default error message', () => {\n    render(<ErrorState />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(/Unable to connect to the API server/)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it('renders custom error message', () => {\n    render(<ErrorState message=\"Custom error message\" />);\n    expect(screen.getByText('Custom 